# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF on every OS. The build's regenerate-and-compare
# gates (the PostgreSQL baseline, the relay's third-party notices, the CLI's generated client and
# docs) write LF, so a CRLF working copy would read as drift on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch scripts need CRLF to run reliably under cmd.exe.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

*.jar binary
*.png binary
